Upstream SMAUG echo-state bug — echo_on_str sent after the color
preference prompt (in CON_GET_WANT_RIPANSI) instead of before it
(at the end of CON_CONFIRM_NEW_PASSWORD).  The user types the
password retype with echo off, then the color preference prompt
appears, but echo is still off — the user's "ANSI"/"RIP"/"none"
selection is invisible until they hit return.  Move the IAC
WONT ECHO so it is sent immediately after the password is
confirmed, before the next prompt.

This is a SMAUG bug, not a madc workaround, but lives here for the
same reason the rest of the patches do: the upstream tarball is the
authoritative source and we don't fork it.

--- a/upstream/smaug1.8/src/comm.c
+++ b/upstream/smaug1.8/src/comm.c
@@ -1890,13 +1890,13 @@
 	    return;
 	}

+	write_to_buffer( d, echo_on_str, 0 );
 	write_to_buffer( d, "\n\rPlease select your color preference\n\r ANSI\n\r RIP\n\r No color support\n\r: ", 0 );
 	d->connected = CON_GET_WANT_RIPANSI;
         break;


     case CON_GET_WANT_RIPANSI:
-	write_to_buffer( d, echo_on_str, 0 );
 	switch ( argument[0] )
 	{
 	case 'r': case 'R':
